    "text": "<p>Nitrous acid gives nitrosonium ion as electrophile&nbsp;(<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>NO</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math>)&nbsp;which attacks phenol at less hindered p-position of form p-nitrosophenol.&nbsp; The nitroso group undergo reduction and forms amine in the presence of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mi>SH</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0063_eb4fe6afaa5a.png\" style=\"width: 613px; height: 112px;\" /></p>"
